{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for task/ui-thread-temporary-discussion at exact head\n019f08ba02905c71acd2fde28c10d262b3381456.\n\nThe feature is well factored and its pure helpers are genuinely pinned. Two\nuser-visible defects and one evidence gap stand between it and merge.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, AND HOW\n\nCheckout. The reviewed worktree\n/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/ui-thread-temporary-discussion sits at\n019f08ba02905c71acd2fde28c10d262b3381456 with an empty `git status\n--porcelain`; `git diff --check` is clean; the single commit carries\n`Rests-On: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:14ddcb02dda7cc6be102b18e4db413a75e519f6f`.\n\nBundle. In a detached scratch worktree at the head, `npm ci \u0026\u0026 npm run build`\nleft `git status --porcelain` empty and re-emitted the committed asset name\nindex-Dp3xQVxn.js. The committed bundle is the output of its sources.\n\nGates. `make vet`, `make test`, `make race` (go test -race ./...) and `make\nbuild` all pass at the head.\n\nTests. Baseline `npm test` is 39/39. I then ran seventeen mutation\nexperiments in the scratch worktree, each reverting one behaviour and\nre-running the suite. Eleven were caught; six survived. Details below.\n\nServer side. The diff contains no Go source changes, so expiry stays\nnexus-owned. I read the path anyway: /v0/say copies `about` verbatim into the\nframe body (spike/internal/service/server.go:239), and Hub.PublishForSession\nkeys one conversation per exact `about`\n(spike/internal/nexus/nexus.go:393-406), so exact-event isolation holds at the\nserver as well as in the client. Promotion is unchanged: discussion messages\nin the pane expose cite only, feeding the room composer's evidence list.\n\nFINDING 1 — the optimistic echo never clears in the default view\nui/src/App.tsx:30, ui/src/App.tsx:134-150, ui/src/components/Stream.tsx:85-91\n\nReconciliation lives in one place: the effect in Stream that calls\n`onReconcile`. `onReconcile` is passed to Stream and nowhere else. Stream is\nmounted only when `mainView === \"activity\"` (App.tsx:136), and `mainView`\ninitialises to `\"work\"` (App.tsx:30). The event thread pane is reachable from\nthe Work view (App.tsx:134, WorkDrawer.tsx:173 and :203) and, after this\nchange, accepts Temporary replies there.\n\nSo on the default screen a temporary reply sent from an event thread adds a\npending echo that nothing is mounted to retire. The delivered frame arrives\nand renders in the discussion list while the italic echo stays beneath it —\nthe same words twice, permanently, until the reader switches to Activity or\nreloads. Before this change the temporary path existed only for frame threads,\nwhich are reachable only from the stream itself, so Stream was always mounted\nwhen an echo could be created. The change moves the echo somewhere Stream is\nnot.\n\nProved by experiment: an SSR render of ThreadPane holding one delivered frame\n(\"same words twice\", about event-one) plus its matching pending item renders\nthe text twice and keeps the `aria-label=\"sending temporary reply\"` element.\n\nFINDING 2 — nested replies under an event-anchored frame render nowhere\nui/src/lib/interaction.ts (eventDiscussionFrames, frameBelongsInRoom),\nui/src/components/ThreadPane.tsx:224-234, ui/src/components/Stream.tsx:266\n\nA frame carrying `re` is excluded from the room by `frameBelongsInRoom` and\nexcluded from the event pane by the `!frame.re` filter in\n`eventDiscussionFrames`. Its parent's thread pane is the only place left, and\nthat pane can no longer be opened: `onOpenThread({kind: \"frame\", …})` appears\nexactly once in the codebase, on the room's MessageLine (Stream.tsx:266), and\nevent-anchored parents no longer reach the room. The pane's ThreadMessage\ncarries a cite button only.\n\nTwo consequences. Inside the UI, temporary discussion on an event is flat with\nno reply affordance, so `temporaryReplyDelivery`'s frame branch — the code the\nrequest asks to preserve — is unreachable for exactly the frames this feature\ncreates. Outside it, an MCP client can still send `say {about: \u003cevent\u003e, re:\n\u003cframe\u003e}`, and that message now renders in no view at all.\n\nProved by experiment: SSR probes at the head. The room shows neither the\nanchored parent nor its nested reply, and shows an ordinary \"the workroom\"\nline normally; the event pane shows the parent and not the reply. (Rendering\nStream under SSR required stubbing `globalThis.document` — see finding 3.)\n\nFINDING 3 — the suite cannot fail on several conditions the report claims met\n\nSeventeen mutants, six survivors, all six on behaviour named in the request:\n\n  SURVIVED  Stream's room filter reverted to the pre-change `if (frame.re)\n            continue;` — the room-side half of \"event conversations cannot mix\n            across thread IDs\" is unpinned.\n  SURVIVED  Stream's reconcile reverted to author+text only — the exact\n            cross-thread echo cancellation `pendingMatchesFrame` exists to\n            prevent can be reintroduced with 39/39 green.\n  SURVIVED  `setText(line)` removed from the temporary-send catch — the report\n            claims \"restores retry text\"; no test can see it.\n  SURVIVED  `setError(...)` removed from the same catch — the report claims\n            \"exposes an accessible error\"; no test can see it.\n  SURVIVED  the expired-conversation guard removed from ThreadComposer.\n  SURVIVED  the send button's temporary/kept accessible name replaced with a\n            constant.\n\n  CAUGHT    eventDiscussionFrames dropping `!frame.re`; dropping the event\n            anchor; pendingForThread dropping the event anchor;\n            pendingMatchesFrame always true; temporaryReplyDelivery losing the\n            exact anchor; sendTemporaryReply not calling `failed`;\n            frameBelongsInRoom not excluding event-anchored frames; the event\n            thread defaulting to Temporary; the Kept/Temporary toggle losing\n            its accessible name; the discussion list removed from the pane.\n\nThe pattern is clean: everything extracted into ui/src/lib/interaction.ts is\nwell covered, and everything left wired inside Stream.tsx and ThreadComposer\nis covered by nothing. Part of the reason is mechanical and worth stating,\nbecause it will shape the fix: Stream cannot be rendered by the existing\nharness at all. It reads `document.title` during render\n(ui/src/components/Stream.tsx:75), so `vite.ssrLoadModule` plus\n`renderToStaticMarkup` throws `document is not defined`. I could only observe\nthe room-side behaviour by stubbing `globalThis.document` in a scratch probe.\nA committed test needs that shim or a small refactor moving the title read\ninto the effect that uses it.\n\nFINDING 4 — the room loses its live talk with nothing left to say so\n\nWorth a decision rather than a silent consequence. Of the ten frames live in\nthis workroom right now, all ten are anchored to durable event ids, and every\nanchor matches a `projection.statements` entry exactly. At this head the room\nstream therefore renders zero chat lines. Meanwhile the event card's\nThreadIndicator counts durable provenance children only\n(buildThreadIndex.summary in ui/src/lib/threads.ts), so nothing on the card\nsignals that an event has temporary discussion. Talk becomes reachable only by\nopening the right thread and finding it there. The isolation is what was\nasked for; the absent signal is the part I think needs an answer before merge.\n\nOBSERVATIONS I DELIBERATELY DID NOT RAISE AS FINDINGS\n\n- main is not an ancestor. The merge-base is edb53ce; the branch was eleven\n  commits behind when I began and main has since moved to c24359e, which\n  promoted the shipping module to the repository root. The branch touches only\n  ui/ and spike/internal/service/uidist/, and main's commits since the\n  merge-base touch only Go and docs paths, so there is no content conflict —\n  but spike/internal/service/uidist/ no longer exists on main, so the merge\n  will have to re-emit the bundle under internal/service/uidist/. Not a defect\n  in the work; a re-integration step before step 5.\n- \"Temporary discussion · 0 messages\" renders on every event thread, empty or\n  not. The aria-label on that separator div has no role to attach to and is\n  not exposed to assistive technology, though its visible text is read.\n- Before the projection loads, `durableEvents` is empty, so event-anchored\n  frames render in the room for one paint and then vanish.\n- Frames are collected across all live conversations (ui/src/lib/frames.ts),\n  so the new per-event conversations are delivered without further work.\n\nWHAT I COULD NOT VERIFY\n\nBrowser runtime behaviour. The repository has no DOM test harness — jsdom,\nhappy-dom and testing-library are all absent from ui/package.json — so\nfindings 1 and 2 rest on structural proof plus SSR renders rather than a live\nclick-through. I did not exercise the real /v0/say round trip from a browser.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f06285a018bc5806a8fe8732d9c91fd240807e1c","head":"019f08ba02905c71acd2fde28c10d262b3381456","verdict":"changes-requested"}}